    <title>Vertical Line Test</title> 
      <statement>
        <p component="b" workspace="2in">
          <nbsp />
        </p>
        <p component="a">
          If any vertical line crosses...
        </p>
      </statement>
    </definition>
    <example workspace="5in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          For each of the graphs below, determine if they correspond to graphs of functions?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </example>
  </paragraphs>
</page>
<page>
  <paragraphs>
    <title>Finding Domains</title>
    <p workspace="2in">
      Recall the definition of domain from earlier:
    </p>
    <example workspace="2in">
      <statement>
        <p>
          For the function <md>f(x) = \frac{\sqrt{x} + 2}{x-4}</md>, evaluate <m>f(0)</m>, <m>f(2)</m>, <m>f(4)</m>, <m>f(-3)</m>. What is the domain of this function?
        </p>
      </statement>
    </example>
    <p workspace="2in">
      What do we need to be concerned about when trying to determine the domain of a function?
    </p>
  </paragraphs>
</page>
<page>
  <example workspace="1in">
    <introduction>
      <p>
        For each of the functions below, find their domain.
      </p>
    </introduction>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          <md>f(x) = \frac{1}{x+3}</md>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          <md>f(x) = \frac{x^2 + 4x + 5}{x^2 + 2x - 8}</md>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          <md>f(x) = x^2 + \sqrt{x^2 + 1}</md>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          <md>f(x) = \sqrt{x^2 - 4}</md>
        </p>
      </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
      <statement>
        <p>
          <md>f(x) = \sqrt[3]{x+2}</md>
        </p>
